  "What's the CAGR of median gaming early-stage VC deal value and pre-money valuation ($M) in the segment of development?": {
    "answer": "To calculate the Compound Annual Growth Rate (CAGR) for both the median gaming early-stage VC deal value and pre-money valuation in the development segment, we use the formula:\n\n\\[ \\text{CAGR} = \\left( \\frac{\\text{Ending Value}}{\\text{Beginning Value}} \\right)^{\\frac{1}{\\text{n}}} - 1 \\]\n\nwhere:\n- Ending Value is the value at the end of the period,\n- Beginning Value is the value at the beginning of the period,\n- n is the number of years.\n\n**Deal Value CAGR Calculation:**\n\nBeginning Value (2020) = $5.4M\nEnding Value (2025) = $4.3M\nn = 5 years\n\n\\[ \\text{CAGR} = \\left( \\frac{4.3}{5.4} \\right)^{\\frac{1}{5}} - 1 \\]\n\n\\[ \\text{CAGR} = (0.7963)^{0.2} - 1 \\]\n\n\\[ \\text{CAGR} = 0.9706 - 1 \\]\n\n\\[ \\text{CAGR} = -0.0294 \\]\n\n\\[ \\text{CAGR} = -2.94\\% \\]\n\n**Pre-money Valuation CAGR Calculation:**\n\nBeginning Value (2020) = $15.0M\nEnding Value (2025) = $155.9M\nn = 5 years\n\n\\[ \\text{CAGR} = \\left( \\frac{155.9}{15.0} \\right)^{\\frac{1}{5}} - 1 \\]\n\n\\[ \\text{CAGR} = (10.3933)^{0.2} - 1 \\]\n\n\\[ \\text{CAGR} = 2.589 - 1 \\]\n\n\\[ \\text{CAGR} = 1.589 \\]\n\n\\[ \\text{CAGR} = 158.9\\% \\]\n\nTherefore, the CAGR for the median gaming early-stage VC deal value in the development segment over the period from 2020 to 2025 is -2.94%, indicating a decrease, while the CAGR for the pre-money valuation is 158.9%, indicating a significant increase.",
